  "name": "Smash Lock uses its authored caster-level bonus on real lockboxes (#6730)",
  "contract": "Smash Lock 570122 has EffectBasePoints 4 + DieSides 1, RealPointsPerLevel 5, BaseLevel 1 and SpellLevel 16: its native bonus is 5 + 5*(level-16), not an invented level*5 rule. Thus a level-38 Barbarian without skill 633 has bonus 115 and opens Iron Lockbox 4634 (Lock 24, requires 70), but cannot open Strong Iron Lockbox 4636 (Lock 60, requires 125). At level 45 the bonus is 150, safely above the random orange-lock failure band for the 125 lock. Actual native container opening exposes loot after unlocking. Ordinary Rogue Pick Lock still uses trained Lockpicking 100, opening the 70 lock and refusing the 125 lock. No Barbarian Lockpicking skill is granted. A native Truesilver Skeleton Key item keeps its constant 200 skill bonus, consumes one key when opening the 125 lock and refuses the 225 lock without consuming another.",
